    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The internet is not unfamiliar to most of us in Shanghai. But around half of the world’s population still can’t connect to the internet. Big companies like SpaceX want to change this. They plan to launch special "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "satellites",
            "ref": "v-satellite"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " into "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "orbit",
            "zh": "轨道"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". These satellites will be able to “"
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "broadcast",
            "ref": "v-broadcast"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "” the net across the Earth. But there is another "
          },
          {
            "t": "underline",
            "v": "problem to be solved before more people can enjoy using the internet"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "There are thousands of different languages spoken around the world. Most things on the web, however, are only available in a few of them. For example, about five per cent of the world speaks English at home, but around 50 per cent of the web is in English. When some people go online, they may find that the internet offers little in their own language."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Many major online platforms were founded in the United States. They started with English-speaking users. As the internet has continued to develop around the world, these companies have been forced to play catch-up. Facebook has been "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "criticised",
            "ref": "v-criticise"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for its slow pace. Take Myanmar"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "",
            "zh": "缅甸"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", one of its new markets, as an example. The company had only a few native editors for years. Without good editors, "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "misinformation",
            "ref": "v-misinformation"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " started to spread across its platform."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Some companies have been trying to bring smaller languages online. Mozilla, for example, is working on Common Voice. The project collects recordings from people speaking English and German, as well as those speaking Sinhala and Yoruba. It can be used to train AI programs to help edit things online."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Meanwhile, companies like Google are developing better translation programs. These programs can make it easier to use the internet in different languages. However, it is very difficult, if not impossible, to translate things like jokes."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
